  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Project Setup**\n\nI\'m currently assessing the initial project setup. I see a `package.json`, an `App.tsx` file, and `metadata.json`. It\'s a React project, and the existence of a `package.json` strongly suggests npm or yarn. I will next investigate the contents of the files to understand the project\'s structure, the libraries included, and the components defined. I am planning on checking the dependencies and scripts defined, as well as the imports and components that are already implemented.\n\n\n**Evaluating Image Assets**\n\nI\'ve shifted focus to the image assets for the AETHER ARCHITECTURE app. The provided HTML contains hotlink URLs, so image generation isn\'t needed. I am now confirming the URLs for the Home screen\'s hero image and other screen elements within the provided HTML. I\'m reviewing the skills available and found no need for image-generation and UI-related skills.\n\n\n**Identifying Image Assets**\n\nI\'ve begun cataloging the image assets within the provided HTML. I\'ve noted URLs for the Services section and a testimonial client named Budi Santoso, as well as an article image. I\'m focused on correctly mapping each image URL. I\'m aiming to create a comprehensive list.\n\n\n**Cataloging Image URLs**\n\nI\'m now identifying image URLs for articles and the \"About Us\" screen. Article 2 uses `https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/aida-public/AB6AXuC8hrLAHARTx3Nk4AiKlxRZarI0qnOegNcOv1VIolM8TjGSyA8O16dIIa6YyTFx2Aj_Xh9LqARz5ioPO6Y4rjhBcDvkpcoEX9LoHnEDiwmRt2A8S2bg1keoQmnLCfIPAFEY6tGJjEjXeras1oHNZix7hxIM_8Q4oT0s5Ro_UT5y7eXNR2k7h8sl63izBg26kloRzXRSe84tcS93P7uTDTc-oe2GiVb3l0f5wM0PmwiYz18FK63RMc-i`, and Article 3 uses `https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/aida-public/AB6AXuDdVYPPkxIiaMAWyhejSpH-Nl008UIebdl7IYvPvGdZ8c0aOUYQDaaYaO30omlh1HQ29KuZRC9Gcf6Nsyj9eiv8GS-romNqP89a_a1XpHdIhkuYmq00jxcyaxDMcNTRdQXPWh-7duGxHIbO-H0oMcDhnQYFSslZNV0DUw5-6Ktb4rvcaTK95GBc9NF8vyOqlZrp59XSbkv-YgJBeE71RHIJN9fyCaO6v58rKfjZNufGFNffYc-NXCvO`. Adrian Wijaya is using `https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/aida-public/AB6AXuAyutdWxO0xpYkftSWpyVITRA6cb1F-biCWl`.\n\n\n**Compiling Image Data**\n\nI\'ve just added three more image URLs to the list: for Maya Santoso, Budi Pratama, and Dina Lestari. I am still meticulously tracking and adding each specific image reference in the HTML. I\'m making sure to correlate each URL to its corresponding user or section. The goal is to build a complete inventory.\n\n\n**Gathering Image URLs**\n\nI am now focusing on gathering image URLs. I just added two more URLs from the Portfolio screen: one for \"Pusat Data Zenith\" and another for \"Kantor Pusat Lumina.\" I am working my way through the HTML to build up a full dataset. I have also added an image for the Services Section, focusing on Landscape Architecture.\n\n\n**Expanding Image List**\n\nI\'ve just added three more URLs to my catalog. These cover two new projects, \"Identitas Monolith\" and \"Residensi Vertikal,\" plus a case study on \"Revitalisasi Urban.\" I am methodically identifying and recording each image URL, and I\'m nearing what I consider a thorough collection.\n\n\n**Planning React App Structure**\n\nI\'m now outlining the React application\'s structure. I\'m focusing on navigation with smooth transitions, interactive elements like filter functions for the portfolio, and a dark/light mode toggle. A beautiful and cohesive multi-screen design will incorporate \"Geist\" and \"Inter\" typography. I\'m looking at implementing a contact dialog as well.\n\n\n\n**Defining Navigation Strategy**\n\nMy focus has shifted to defining the navigation strategy. Considering user requirements and the HTML structure, I\'ve confirmed a multi-screen design. I\'ve designed clean navigation that covers \"Services,\" \"Portfolio,\" \"About,\" and \"Blog,\" (displaying the \"Jurnal Desain\" articles). I\'ve made the logo \"AETHER\" redirect to the Home page.\n\n\n**Structuring React App**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing app structure and component separation. Following the provided guidance, I\'m creating dedicated files and implementing the recommended directory structure. I\'m focusing on defining types and separating data and logic to establish a maintainable React application. I\'m adding `types.ts`, `data.ts`, `Header.tsx`, `Footer.tsx`, and views for each screen.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 23
      nanos: 604242147
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
