    summary: "\"AETHER ARCHITECTURE\", \"Ruang Bentuk Tujuan,\" and \"Pusat Data Zenith\" refer to various concepts and entities across architecture, design, and data infrastructure.\n\n**AETHER ARCHITECTURE** encompasses several distinct entities and projects:\n*   **Aether Architects** is an architectural practice founded in 2015 by Zelin Huang in Shenzhen, China. This firm is recognized for its sensitive approach to natural phenomena, perception, and the interrelationships between space, matter, and the human body, with notable projects including the Air-Mountain Pavilion and Enclave Book Pavilion.[1]\n*   **Aether Studio**, established in 2012 in New York, focuses on creating innovative, sustainable, and timeless designs for residential, commercial, and urban environments.[2]\n*   **Aether Architecture** also describes a practice that specializes in interactive architecture systems and dynamic graphical interfaces, merging spatial design with technology to craft cultural experiences. Their work often involves creating responsive, media-rich spaces for public installations.[3][4]\n*   An architectural project named **Aether** in the Antarctic Peninsula aims to reconnect humanity with the night sky. This design incorporates a monumental opening called \"The Rift\" and utilizes sustainable wind energy.[5][6]\n*   **Aether: Living Architecture Software Suite** is a software system designed to support various living architecture constructions, enabling physical installations to exhibit lifelike behaviors through virtual ecosystems and graphical interfaces.[7]\n*   An **Aether Data Center** located in Phoenix, Arizona, is a 40,000 square foot facility comprising a computer data and network operations center, alongside offices and conference rooms. Vertrees Architecture & Engineering Services provided design coordination and project management for this center.[8]\n*   \"AETHER\" also refers to a cinematic landing page template for architecture and design studios, emphasizing spatial flow and material honesty through immersive scroll-driven animations.[9]\n\n**Ruang Bentuk Tujuan** (Space, Form, Purpose/Goal) are fundamental concepts, particularly within architectural and design discourse in Indonesian contexts:\n*   **Ruang** (space) is understood as the distance between two objects, creating an area and width, and is a critical element in graphic art, interior design, and architecture. Space can be two-dimensional (dwimatra) or three-dimensional (trimatra).[10][11][12]\n*   In architecture, **fungsi** (function), **ruang** (space), **bentuk** (form), and **ekspresi bentuk** (form expression) are considered interconnected and inseparable, as architecture serves as the physical vessel for human activities.[13]\n*   Space can manifest as real (nyata) or virtual (maya), and as exterior (luar) or interior (dalam) space.[14]\n\n**Pusat Data Zenith** (Zenith Data Center) refers to data facilities and related services:\n*   **Zenith Data Center-Loyang Drive** is mentioned in connection with Yeo-Heng, a company that provides services, potentially electrical works, for data centers.[15]\n*   The **Zenith: Roswell, New Mexico Data Center** is part of Zenith Volts Corporation, a company that integrates utility-scale renewable energy, including solar power and advanced battery storage, with digital infrastructure.[16]\n*   **Zenith Systems** offers 24/7 maintenance and expertise for the electrical and technology needs of data centers, from Tier I to Tier III facilities.[17]\n*   Historically, **Zenith Data Systems (ZDS)** was a division of Zenith, founded in 1979, known for selling personal computers.[18]\n\nSources:\n[1] [metalocus.es](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGT6amXF_UKeBgrHg9f6c10SRgiBq7RANPrmF8DUXrYjm6powXw3h4ZKcJH2OQo3cJ7_duWaAlFIRQWOITOmDj_TWaMP1p9sb-tSvXz1lZMA0onlmvBxpWJ5jpISvg1j9i5z3x0oavGK5Y4_tOlIR0=)\n[2] [framer.website](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQH-X9DZ14C-EZ2EbUjy0pLoMjge2dhS5YLstk9I58G7fNgMNKGNJCL_rdRCfGil-jrVafGmb9uPz2y7scqvnpf_otmQWO1s20I2GL5LMYJs3hMjy8RpWk_lAN7z_cNmLQ==)\n[3] [aether.hu](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQG_4DEr5JSPP_o0IknLhlTEuU5YsAIcr4h2OamOue-zUE0PDIz9-grNPsdMamht948S6D6Mb8PtK4qHPQdJh0PBFbjZ4QYzFBSqgZSe876jUw==)\n[4] [aether.hu](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQH4xH_esoFiIUTN5u_4mZGwWC2yWspaMemh-Vg4A1FsjptMVGM0yTEOYX-mE1X5DFEPp9ORqIjihgcrkVOxn_ApdG9oCzH_qO7ypgYyf-M5tzDacrTtguUigXts)\n[5] [architecturehunter.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGUYWDoNAuYE71aayn7RntNKHaIzsBJL8T4QS8yEkV-7OmHDzzKxECkkl5PsVSUHDYzHeu7vGE3HzKE-MO13ablANq5tPsff_E0lrDJc8Sz-K2GYyVvUgPIjWnNLUA-ndiFu7lAvL6gPFzDDKspR1WoGFkL)\n[6] [worldarchitecture.org](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQH3ISZxmndOAlTO-KtcK4WkutkW5dtahu3F5AgRFblxOAWw31RhE4lUbPUYCP8bMWgBaHohhN0CEbgbs61fJg1P52uh8VkgD1TB9iSgSWrin5F0D_XdZi7nOodLA-Qp5leAI85c0X4VWupuBrmlFSIvLuqA8Pp9KsGs3tJmCPh5LIvNhogN2ZDrDyoS-rcS)\n[7] [livingarchitecturesystems.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGRB1Koeso2pJ3euCOKk676f5j_UZheT5UsbdZbpRYuu1PS6V9f73k24KoPyEt2tB0M_ZCphTNr6TxWh5JeCv0wqHiBz57yZMUozPm483CrRINUEqomVquikM6b-2RE5kLaN5lYYbYE_ctPui66NWrWOJ2hyQ==)\n[8] [vertreesae.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHHNXm2Ihl6SPvh4UkqrMYdmw612VFbvEe7FBQbJfyV4MovzVZuJR-Wc2hpaOUa976kJzqf9xZXwp2Mfpts_6IMP7ecDMBNSdQdeiox1RY4tyELGB9hoAnHujEJZVhVCnocLY9Zc0TJhO8lkdTMtMD2)\n[9] [aura.build](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQE5f6qfr6H2UXgjThCfgM9uicxjYjKL6oSYMNO65fK207zzvyJydKNAaa7Z7_cY7fkzUjlZyhJpqTEjAqvhj41k-8HYK4tdjIvz3fk9GSPYJ53IaAWrJbSGF8gcM3JZxtalLR2dsLOPnSTDAmAi45ta)\n[10] [binus.ac.id](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEArB5kabx5x-ilYljmPGXg8P0FXpL7tbIZa9P3iduFSPmAbx-P8DhgxplJ4evMistihZVFBiuhc2