  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering Dashboard Features**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the need for an admin dashboard to manage submitted projects, visualizing the entire post-submission workflow. I\'m exploring potential features and components, like project status tracking, client communication integration, and task assignment capabilities. This panel\'s primary function will be to oversee the journey of a client\'s project.\n\n\n**Analyzing App Architecture**\n\nI\'m now diving into the current architecture of the React app. Right now, it\'s a client-side application using Vite with no backend or database. Submissions are handled locally within `ContactModal.tsx`, using a local state array (`inquiryHistory`). I am now considering how to restructure this to share inquiry data between the client form and the proposed Admin Panel, and this has led me to explore potential options for where to store submitted inquiries so they can be viewed. I am also determining how the admin panel will be accessed within the app.\n\n\n**Expanding Inquiry Definition**\n\nI\'ve updated the `Inquiry` interface in `src/types.ts` to include a status field for tracking project progress, directly addressing the admin/project manager workflow. I\'m adding statuses like \'Pending\', \'Reviewing\', and \'Approved\', along with fields for admin notes and assignment to team members. This will provide a core function for project management.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will view the `src/types.ts` file first to see how `Inquiry` is structured and update it to support a status flow."
