    thinking: "**Examining Shared State**\n\nI\'m currently focused on how `ContactModal` handles its inquiries. Right now, the `inquiryHistory` is localized within `ContactModal.tsx`. My idea is to move this state to `App.tsx` for shared access, passing down `inquiries` and `setInquiries`. This seems like a better approach for managing inquiries.\n\n\n**Refining Data Flow**\n\nNow, I\'m thinking about the mechanics of updating the shared state. I\'ll pass an `onAddInquiry` function to `ContactModal` as a prop. This function will be called whenever a new inquiry is submitted, updating the global `inquiries` state in `App.tsx`. We will persist this new shared state to `localStorage`. I\'m also thinking of seeding some initial default inquiries to make the dashboard look nicer on first load.\n\n\n**Analyzing Project Details**\n\nI\'m currently reviewing two project details. One involves zoning in Bandung Utara with a 40% KDB and kinetic facade possibilities, estimated for 6-12 months. The other is a bioclimatic villa design in Dago Pakar, approved for a 3-6 month timeline, with an upcoming site visit and plans for a bored pile foundation. I\'m focusing on the environmental approach.\n\n\n**Developing Admin View**\n\nI\'m now focused on building the `AdminView` component and where it fits within the directory structure. I\'m leaning toward `/src/components/AdminView.tsx` for its location. I\'m also thinking of how to style this component. It has to be gorgeous and highly polished.\n\n\n**Designing Admin Dashboard**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the visual design and functionality of the `AdminView` tabs. The first tab, Inbox (Permohonan Masuk), will display a list of all inquiries with key details and a split-view or modal for rich, actionable information. This will include Client Profile, Tapak & Parameter, and Project Manager controls like lead assignment, status updates, priority setting, timeline estimation, internal notes, and a new interactive flow chart/checklist generator to manage project onboarding phases.\n\n\n**Constructing New Features**\n\nI\'m now diving into feature design for the admin dashboard, thinking about automated client communication. I\'m focusing on a notification draft generator that crafts studio letters based on project status, lead architect, and timeline. I\'m also considering a Kanban pipeline board, and an analytics panel with visual cards to display key financial stats and project phases. I think the key will be ease of use.\n\n\n**Calculating Dashboard Metrics**\n\nI\'m now calculating key metrics for the admin dashboard\'s analytics panel. I\'m focusing on revenue, including a rolling 6-month sum, approval rates, a visual breakdown of project classifications (Komersial, Residensial, Urban), and architect workload bars. I\'m also reviewing files to be modified, including adding a PM portal link.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will create a new file `src/components/AdminView.tsx` which implements the complete Project Manager Portal. It features summary metrics, an interactive client inbox with status controls, lead architect assignment, priority toggles, internal review notes, an interactive onboarding flow checklist, dynamic client letter drafts, a visual Kanban pipeline board, and a workload analytics section."
