t, creates poor contrast, which needs to be addressed. The gradient overlay\'s transparency also contributes to this, leaving sections of the text with insufficient backing. I\'m considering using a much darker overlay. A dark wash like `bg-black/40` or a gradient with higher opacity is a very promising starting point. I want to ensure elements have high contrast with their background.\n\n\n**Optimizing Contrast Further**\n\nI\'m now very confident that using `5 to-black/60 dark:from-bg-dark dark:via-black/75 dark:to-black/85` will significantly improve text readability. I\'m focusing on the \"AETHER ARCHITECTURE STUDIO\" badge now, considering that `text-muted-light` is likely a dark gray. I\'m leaning toward using `text-white` or `text-gray-100` for excellent visibility, or `text-primary-dark`, or even `text-white/90`. I\'m then assessing the `RUANG. BENTUK. TUJUAN.` heading, specifically the `TUJUAN.` segment\'s `text-muted-light`, and how it might be strengthened.\n\n\n**Refining Text Highlighting**\n\nI\'m now determining the best color for \"TUJUAN.\" I\'m deciding `text-white/80 dark:text-primary-dark/80` offers the best visibility and a good balance in both light and dark modes. I\'m also confirming the paragraph\'s readability with `text-gray-200` by ensuring a darker `bg-black/50 dark:bg-black/75` overlay. I\'m satisfied now that I\'m setting a proper, dark foundation.\n\n\n**Adjusting Image Brightness**\n\nI\'m now revising the image\'s brightness settings to improve overall contrast and readability. I\'ve decided to reduce the initial brightness to `brightness-60` and `dark:brightness-40` for improved visual impact, making text easier to discern against the background. I\'m confident that these subtle adjustments will significantly enhance the user experience.\n\n\n**Enhancing Contrast Overlay**\n\nI\'m now implementing adjustments to the background gradient. I\'m increasing the opacity of the overlay to ensure high contrast for text elements. I\'m changing `from-bg-light via-transparent to-black/20` to a darker gradient, `from-bg-light via-black/40 to-black/60 dark:from-bg-dark dark:via-black/60 dark:to-black/80`, which strengthens contrast across the entire hero section. I also want to make sure my badge\'s text is legible.\n\n\n**Improving Text Legibility**\n\nI\'m now focusing on line 46, specifically the `TUJUAN.` segment within the heading. I\'m modifying `text-muted-light` to `text-white/70` to boost contrast and enhance its secondary emphasis. Similarly, I\'m updating the paragraph\'s color on line 49, from `dark:text-muted-dark` to `text-gray-200 dark:text-gray-300`, to ensure consistent readability against the darkened hero background. This will resolve issues with the low-contrast of the original text.\n\n\n"
